  "content": {
    "component": "news_article",
    "_uid": "1242-root",
    "title": "ISMC on the Future of Islamic Archaeology in Egypt",
    "subtitle": null,
    "summary": "Dr Stéphane Pradines speaking on the future of Islamic archaeology in Egypt.",
    "media": [
      {
        "_uid": "70c4a74123d852f4",
        "component": "news_media",
        "role": "banner",
        "filename": "1242-BannerImage.jpg",
        "src": "/news-media/1242-BannerImage.jpg",
        "media_type": "image",
        "caption": null,
        "alt": "ISMC on the Future of Islamic Archaeology in Egypt"
      }
    ],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Stéphane Pradines, ISMC associate professor, was invited by the French Institute of Archaeology in Cairo (IFAO) to participate in a debate on the future of Islamic archaeology in Egypt. "
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The seminar was organised by Marie-Odile Rousset (CNRS, Lyon) and Nicolas Michel (Director of the Arab Studies, IFAO)."
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "His presentation included the results of 17 years of research in Fatimid Cairo, exposing the problems that he and his team faced in organising salvage and rescue excavations in a large city. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "He also presented the positive inputs of his field school of Islamic archaeology, the biggest field school for the medieval period organised in Egypt and the Middle East."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
